From 655dae14cde960b97014c53636f2a58a4d53ad7d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Peripheral Pretender setup <pp-setup@localhost>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 22:45:18 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] hw/misc: the DC Motor Click, DRV8833 behind a 74HC4053

click-dcmotor watches PWM, SELECT1 (RST), SELECT2 (CS) and nSLEEP (AN as
a digital pin): the PWM duty is timed on the virtual clock, the
multiplexer picks bridge A or B, and the DRV8833 truth table gives the
drive with fast or slow decay, brake and coast. nFAULT on INT follows a
"fault" property. A motor with a first-order lag turns behind it; rpm,
drive, state and angle read it. qtest.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
